		{"id":"5b868005a68867bb","type":"text","text":"EXPENSE- COLUMN N ADD INSTEAD X ","x":-163,"y":1862,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"54caa99a1aa397fa","type":"text","text":"## Ontology Concepts :\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"unique identifier\",\n  \"name\": \"business name\",\n  \"kind\": \"entity | metric | dimension | dq_rule\",\n  \"description\": \"business explanation\",\n  \"domain\": \"business domain\",\n  \"expression\": \"formula in the format result = operand1 operator operand2\",\n  \"embedding_input\": \"detailed narrative for semantic search\"\n}\n\n\n \n```","x":1920,"y":-540,"width":828,"height":400},
		{"id":"ff923ad994fa796c","type":"text","text":"Step 1: Ontology Concepts (pure domain)\n        ↓ (human / automated approval)\nStep 2: Ontology Relations (concept-to-concept only)\n        ↓\nStep 3: Concept Binding (ontology → metadata)\n        ↓\nStep 4: DQ Rules (bound + relational)\n","x":-1460,"y":635,"width":568,"height":204},
		{"id":"737d6c3c9cecef38","type":"text","text":"## Ontology Relations :\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"uuid\",\n  \"concept_id\": \"uuid from input concept\",\n  \"kind\": \"entity|metric|dimension|dq_rule\",\n  \"concept_expression\": \"formula in format result = operand1 operator operand2 or null for entities\",\n  \"business_fields\": [\n    {\n      \"field_id\": \"uuid\",\n      \"field_name\": \"business field name\",\n      \"field_type\": \"string|numeric|date|boolean|enum\",\n      \"required_for\": \"computation|validation|aggregation|reporting\",\n      \"description\": \"human-friendly explanation of the field\",\n      \"embedding_input\": \"detailed description for this specific field including field_name, field_type, required_for, description, how it relates to the concept, and how it supports the concept_expression\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"domain\": \"business domain or subject area\",\n  \"embedding_input\": \"comprehensive description including ALL concept details (Concept ID, Concept Name, Concept Kind, Domain, Description, Detailed Context, Concept Expression) and all business fields with their purposes, relationships, and FP&A/GL usage context\"\n}\n```","x":1920,"y":-80,"width":1120,"height":620},
		{"id":"f5f2f46c77dd2925","type":"text","text":"## Concept Binding :\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"02c2eac9-2ae9-4b3c-ba2d-2d7daf4a33ae\",\n  \"concept_id\": \"ent_trial_balance\",\n  \"relation_id\": \"b1e1c3f4-5f8e-4c9b-8c1e-3f8e1c3f4b8e\",\n  \"kind\": \"entity\",\n  \"expression\": \"\",\n  \"data_object_id\": [\n    {\n      \"business_field_id\": \"\",\n      \"business_field_name\": \"\",\n      \"description\": \"\",\n      \"field_expression\": \"\",\n      \"mapped_metadta\": [\n      {\n       \"column_id\": \"\",\n       \"column_name\": \"\",\n       \"description\": \"\",\n   },\n   {\n    \"column_id\": \"\",\n       \"column_name\": \"\",\n       \"description\": \"\",\n   }\n      ],\n    },\n    {\n      \"business_field_id\": \"\",\n      \"business_field_name\": \"\",\n      \"description\": \"\",\n      \"field_expression\": \"\",\n      \"mapped_metadta\": [\n      {\n       \"column_id\": \"\",\n       \"column_name\": \"\",\n       \"description\": \"\",\n   },\n   {\n    \"column_id\": \"\",\n       \"column_name\": \"\",\n       \"description\": \"\",\n   }\n      ],\n    }\n  ],\n\n  \"confidence_score\": 0.85,\n  \"status\": \"active\",\n  \"inferred_by\": \"llm\",\n  \"embedding_input\": \"\",\n  \"embedding_vector\": [],\n    \"created_at\": {\n    \"$date\": \"2025-12-17T12:14:20.346Z\"\n  },\n  \"updated_at\": {\n    \"$date\": \"2025-12-17T12:14:20.346Z\"\n  }\n}\n```","x":1920,"y":660,"width":1820,"height":1480},
		{"id":"131ffa29e39f5788","x":960,"y":-540,"width":543,"height":308,"type":"text","text":"Inference steps:\n1. client on boarding - Context / Domain addition \n2. Infer Ontology concepts\n3. Infer Relations on Ontology concepts\n4. Existing Meta inference \n\t1. With New ontology inputs \n5. New API for Binding Physical and conceptual fields. "},
		{"id":"b2b10f71f7f49363","x":5660,"y":-10,"width":380,"height":226,"type":"text","text":"Input \n1. Business fields -\n\t1. age  (1:n)  (age = current year - dob )\n\t2. id - (1:1) ( customer id - cust_id)\n2. Current table metadata with embedding inputs. - files vena\n"},
		{"id":"51aa3ea681439d69","x":5300,"y":-40,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"Ontology relations"},
		{"id":"42eff879729d7fa1","x":5300,"y":203,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"Table metadata - customer\norder, claim"},
		{"id":"1555450144b485aa","x":6240,"y":73,"width":341,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"Build a semantic Query (query to retrieve)"},
		{"id":"3f65329fdc76e7a3","x":6161,"y":-496,"width":500,"height":486,"type":"text","text":"LLM 1 prompt\n\n1. Take the input \n2. Merge the input.\n3. Query building \n\t1. first ask llm whether the given input business field leads to one to one match or does it needs certain computations to map the business field. (mainly entity kind will lead to one to one mappings, and rest kinds leads to computations of several columns to business field ).\n\t2. If needs computation make a expression for it.\n\t\t1. breakdown each component into a sub query.\n\t3. Consider the fields as searching query \n\t4. Build search query by keeping in mind the current table embedding in hand and on top of it look for those columns. \n\t5. Query built"},
		{"id":"8cb825c0ea573d6b","x":6800,"y":-301,"width":250,"height":97,"type":"text","text":"1. N number of Queries for semantic search\n2. Expression (Optional)"},
		{"id":"071331c88823bf11","x":5000,"y":69,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"Process Starts "},
		{"id":"cc454af9b6085b31","x":6675,"y":73,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"Mongo Semantic Search "},
		{"id":"bb34a91d8f5f871c","x":7050,"y":59,"width":250,"height":89,"type":"text","text":"Retrievals - Top k column match for each query along with embedding "},
		{"id":"27dc62d5eac8beb7","x":7400,"y":74,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"Augment Process "},
		{"id":"4dea91cc8b7ee407","x":7760,"y":58,"width":251,"height":90,"type":"text","text":"Map the physical columns to concept binding along with business field. "},
		{"id":"13f324136b02f990","x":7285,"y":-640,"width":480,"height":543,"type":"text","text":"Frame the input \n1. N number of search queries.\n2. Main business field query ( your agenda of what is that you are looking for)\n\t1. Expression if 1:N ( LLM 1 output)\n3. Current table metadata embedding \n4. The retrieval matched top k columns - attach them to respective sub queries.\n\t1. Use the matched column embedding for critique process down below.\n5. Seek LLM to be a critique and decide what needs to mapped and what needs to rejected. \n6. Process is simple if 1:N mapping requires look for expression of LLM 1 output and map accordingly by keeping in mind the main agenda what is that you are looking for.\n7. Shell out the columns which are mapped along with descriptions. "}
	],
